      ],
      "text": "**For a short trip outside, an N95 isn’t generally necessary if you’re healthy.** But haze is significant today: NEA forecast a 24-hour PSI of **150–230** for **Saturday, October 17**—unhealthy to very unhealthy. Limit time outdoors and skip strenuous exercise; consider an N95 if you’ll be outside for a long time, especially if you’re older, pregnant, a child, or have heart or lung disease. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026?utm_source=openai))\n\nCheck NEA’s latest **1-hour PM2.5** reading or the myENV app before heading out, since conditions can vary by area and hour. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026?utm_source=openai))",
